                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "You probably want to add this property to `schemas/gpio_presence.json`,\n\notherwise the configuration cannot pass the validator and the build will fail."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/anacapa/anacapa_scm.json",
                    "line": 281,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks, I moved the schema support for LogPresenceChange into change 88281\n(\"gpio-presence: add configurable presence event logging\") by updating\nschemas/gpio_presence.json."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/anacapa/anacapa_scm.json",
                    "line": 281,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "You need to stack this change on top of 88281 then.\n\n(as in, create a local branch like below, and push that):\n\n88305 change <- HEAD\n88281 change\n\nOtherwise the schema will be missing when CI runs for this change and you cannot get a Verified +1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/anacapa/anacapa_scm.json",
                    "line": 281,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "This revision no longer uses LogPresenceChange, so it no longer depends on 88281."
                }
            ],
